{
  "id": "T-1656",
  "created_at": 1791231210.141526,
  "parent": "T-1654",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: scripts/with-tokens.sh: run a command with allowlisted f-tok tokens in its env, values never printed",
  "spec": "New script scripts/with-tokens.sh in the orchestrator repo: run one command with selected stored tokens in its\nenvironment, never printing a value. Model it on luna-inbox's scripts/with-secrets.sh (read it:\n/Users/k3ntaw/code/luna-inbox/scripts/with-secrets.sh): it sources \"${HOME}/.config/f/f.sh\" and reads\n`f tok get <id> --reveal` into a variable with printf -v, never echoing.\n\nUsage:\n  scripts/with-tokens.sh ENV_NAME=token-id [ENV_NAME=token-id ...] -- command [args...]\n  scripts/with-tokens.sh --list        # prints the allowlisted token ids, one per line, nothing else\n\nRules:\n1. Allowlist: token ids allowed are the non-blank, non-# lines of ${WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST:-<repo root>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt}.\n   Missing or empty allowlist -> every request refused (exit 3, \"with-tokens: no allowlist\"). A token id not on the\n   list -> exit 3 \"with-tokens: <id> is not allowlisted\". The human owns this file; the script never writes it.\n2. ENV_NAME must match ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$ and must not be PATH, HOME, SHELL, IFS, BASH_ENV, ENV, LD_PRELOAD,\n   DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH, PROMPT_COMMAND (exit 2 otherwise). token-id must match ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$.\n3. `--` and a command are required (exit 2 with usage otherwise).\n4. Source \"${WITH_TOKENS_F_SH:-$HOME/.config/f/f.sh}\" (the override exists for tests only). For each pair read the value\n   with `f tok get <id> --reveal 2>/dev/null` into a variable; empty or failed -> exit 1 \"with-tokens: missing or\n   empty token: <id>\" (the id, never the value). Export each value under its ENV_NAME and `exec` the command.\n5. Never write a value to stdout, stderr, a file or a log; no set -x; no `env`/`printenv` in the script.\n   The command's own output is the caller's responsibility (document: never run echo/printenv/env through it).\n6. Header comment: purpose, usage, the allowlist rule, and \"values reach only the child process\".\n\nTests: new tests/test_with_tokens.py (unittest, subprocess, no real secrets): a temp fake f.sh defining\n`f() { [ \"$1 $2\" = \"tok get\" ] && case \"$3\" in a-key) printf secret-a;; b-key) printf secret-b;; *) return 1;; esac; }`\npassed via WITH_TOKENS_F_SH, and a temp allowlist via WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST. Named tests:\n- test_runs_command_with_token_in_env: A=a-key -- python3 -c \"import os;print(len(os.environ['A']))\" prints 8; the\n  value itself never appears in stdout or stderr of the wrapper (assert 'secret-a' not in stderr).\n- test_two_tokens\n- test_not_allowlisted_refused (exit 3, value of no token in output)\n- test_missing_allowlist_refuses_all\n- test_missing_token_exits_1_and_names_id_only\n- test_bad_env_name_refused (lowercase, PATH, LD_PRELOAD)\n- test_requires_double_dash_and_command\n- test_list_prints_allowlist_only\nRun: uv run python -m pytest -q tests/test_with_tokens.py (or unittest). Commit on the task branch.\nDo not touch .claude/hooks, .orchestrator/protected-paths.txt or the allowlist file itself (the human creates it).\n",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1655"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_with_tokens.py: the eight named tests exist and pass",
    "No token value is ever written to stdout, stderr or a file by the script",
    "Without .orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt every request is refused",
    "No change under .claude/hooks or to .orchestrator/protected-paths.txt"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
    "tests/test_with_tokens.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
