      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "The script meets the acceptance criteria. All eight named tests exist as unittest methods, and the file starts with `import _harness`. A missing or empty allowlist exits 3. The script prints no token value and does not use `set -x`, `env` or `printenv`. Only the two scoped files changed, so nothing under .claude/hooks or protected-paths.txt was touched. I read the code and did not run the tests. The gate on the diff reported green.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
            "line": 102,
            "issue": "Sourcing f.sh runs under `set -euo pipefail`. If the real f.sh references unset variables or returns non-zero, the wrapper aborts before the token lookup with no 'with-tokens:' message. A missing f.sh also fails with a bare bash error. Consider an explicit existence check with a clear error, or `set +u` around the source.",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          {
            "path": "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
            "line": 117,
            "issue": "The child inherits WITH_TOKENS_F_SH and WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST from the caller's environment. Neither is a secret, so this is harmless. Unsetting them before exec would keep the child environment clean.",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          {
            "path": "tests/test_with_tokens.py",
            "line": 84,
            "issue": "The invalid token-id case (`A=bad/id`) only asserts exit code 2 and does not check stdout or stderr for leaks. This is minor, since the id is not a secret.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
